cus","title":"Renoise focus","description":"What the producer is looking at in Renoise: {epoch, view, selection, transport, changed}. Cheap enough to poll about every 150 ms; read again only when changed moves.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"focus_body","title":"Renoise view","description":"What Renoise shows in one of its views, ready to draw: pass kind, and ref (the take, track or pattern it is about) or window (the range to show) where the kind takes them. Long ones come in pages: pass the nextCursor as cursor.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["pattern","matrix","phrase","instrument","dsp"],"description":"Which view."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of what the view is about."},"around":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of a track to centre the first page of tracks on (the arrange view): the page starts half a page above it, and says where in `from`."},"window":{"type":"object","properties":{"from":{"type":"number"},"to":{"type":"number"}},"required":["from","to"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The range to show, in the view's own units."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"The nextCursor an earlier page gave, unchanged."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"description":"Rows in a page."},"layout":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"The layout the refs were read in (each answer and tracks event says it): refs from an older one are carried through the track shifts since."},"hidden":{"type":"boolean","description":"Also list data in the note and effect columns the track doesn't show, on every line (under `hidden`). Without it only a line with nothing in the shown columns is looked through."}},"required":["kind"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_preview","title":"Preview a Renoise change","description":"What one change would do in Renoise, without making it: {transactionId, confirmation, prior, display, target, epoch}. Apply it with change_apply.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","description":"The change kind."},"input":{"type":"object","description":"What the kind takes."},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch the refs in input came from."},"layout":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"The layout the refs were read in (each answer and tracks event says it): refs from an older one are carried through the track shifts since."}},"required":["kind","input"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_apply","title":"Apply a Renoise change","description":"Makes a previewed change in Renoise, as one named step of Renoise's undo. The same idempotencyKey again returns the first answer and changes nothing. state is applied, or uncertain when Renoise didn't answer.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"transactionId":{"type":"string"},"confirmation":{"type":"string","description":"The confirmation change_preview gave."},"idempotencyKey":